      "timing_segments": []
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p09",
      "text": "A summary should include the central process and the evidence that supports it. Interesting side details belong only when they help explain that process. A reader can separate the observation from the explanation, then ask whether the cited evidence supports the connection. Recording conditions and repeated results makes the account easier for another person to check.",
      "illustration_brief": "Diagram or scene about animals without printed labels; do not reveal the page's exact wording.",
      "audio_script": "A summary should include the central process and the evidence that supports it. Interesting side details belong only when they help explain that process. A reader can separate the observation from the explanation, then ask whether the cited evidence supports the connection. Recording conditions and repeated results makes the account easier for another person to check.",
      "timing_segments": []
    },
    {
      "page_id": "p10",
      "text": "Understanding the night work of moths therefore depends on observation, measurement, and comparison. These practices turn a visible pattern into an explanation that another person can check. A reader can separate the observation from the explanation, then ask whether the cited evidence supports the connection. Recording conditions and repeated results makes the account easier for another person to check.",
